			<div class="content" id="post-content-2527750">
									

<blockquote>
<p>What about when people have conflicting goals?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This catalyzes teamwork and cooperation, it doesn't literally apply goals . Note that it helped both competing basketball teams as well both the escaping D-Class and the security team that stopped them.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Let’s say a foundation representative and 5 or 6 members of different groups of interest are all given the goal of finding a way that all of them can coexist without any of their goals being compromised.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Each team would have enhanced cooperation. This would probably mean that the lone Foundation operative is at an increased disadvantage. Unless they could bring the parties to negotiate, in which case it would probably make negotiations go more smoothly and the &quot;no compromise&quot; goal would be more swiftly abandoned then it would have otherwise been.</p>

							</div>

								
